  "details": "One user cannot pick up a VRCPickup which is a child of another user's copy of a PlayerObject.\n\nRepro steps. In a new world:\n\n1. Creat Empty.\n\n2. Add `PlayerObject` component.\n\n3. As a child of the empty object, create a Cube.\n\n4. Set the cube's collider to a trigger.\n\n5. Add `VRCPickup` to the cube.\n\n6. Optional: Scale the cube smaller.\n\n7. Optional: Disable the empty game object.\n\n8. Upload & invite a friend, or build & test with 2 clients.\n\n9. Try to pick up both cubes. Ask your friend to do the same.\n\nRecommended solution: Fix the bug, or if this is intentional, add a serialized bool to `PlayerObject` which, when true, allows other users to pick up your PlayerObject's VRCPickup.",
